node_modules

# Environment files hold per-account values, so they stay out of git — except
# "my-account", the one every user starts from. Tracking it leaks nothing, and
# costs nothing: every variable in it is secret-marked, so Bruno keeps the
# values in its own encrypted store and writes only their names into the file.
# Filling it in therefore changes no tracked file at all, which is what keeps a
# user's setup from blocking their next pull.
#
# Note the glob rather than a trailing slash. Git cannot re-include a file
# inside an excluded *directory*, so the negation below only works because the
# rule above excludes the directory's contents instead of the directory itself.
Spacelift/environments/*
!Spacelift/environments/my-account.bru
